{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Interactions.MarkovPeelH3","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Interactions.MarkovPeelH3","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Interactions.MarkovPeel","lean:module:QOU.Interactions.HeckeEngine"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.canonicalMarkovTraceH3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.canonicalMarkovTraceH3","kind":"def","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/MarkovPeelH3.lean#L195-L206","doc":"Canonical instance: take `R = R_q` and embed via `RingHom.id`.\nProvides the full `MarkovTraceH3` record on the H₃ NF basis,\nparameterised by a chosen `z` and `h = q − q⁻¹` in `R_q`.\n\nThe `tr` field is `trH3` applied with the identity ring hom;\nno proofs are bundled into the structure (the four reference\nidentities above suffice for the basis evaluations).  See\n`markov-peel-atomic-tr-m.witness.json` for cross-checks. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.trH3_e_minus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.trH3_e_minus","kind":"theorem","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/MarkovPeelH3.lean#L183-L193","doc":"Reference: tr_M(σ_0 σ_1 σ_0) = h·z² + z.  Hecke quadratic +\nMarkov peel; the only basis element whose trace involves the\nHecke parameter `h`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.trH3_L_plus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.trH3_L_plus","kind":"theorem","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/MarkovPeelH3.lean#L172-L181","doc":"Reference: tr_M(σ_0 σ_1) = z².  Two consecutive Markov peels.\nThis is the H₃ instance of `prop:markov-pair-z2` from the\nabstract typeclass; see `MarkovPeel.markov_pair_z2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.trH3_sigma0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.trH3_sigma0","kind":"theorem","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/MarkovPeelH3.lean#L164-L170","doc":"Reference: tr_M(σ_0) = z.  Single Markov peel from the unit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.trH3_unit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.trH3_unit","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/MarkovPeelH3.lean#L155-L162","doc":"Reference: tr_M(γ) = 1.  Direct from the (M3) unit axiom. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.trH3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.trH3","kind":"def","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/MarkovPeelH3.lean#L105-L153","doc":"The canonical Markov-trace function on H₃ NF basis elements.\n\nGiven Markov parameter `z` and Hecke parameter `h = q − q⁻¹`,\na basis-linear element `a : HeckeNF` (6 coefficients in `R_q`)\nhas Markov trace\n\n  tr (a) = a₀ · 1\n         + a₁ · z          (σ₀)\n         + a₂ · z          (σ₁)\n         + a₃ · z²         (L₊ = σ₀σ₁)\n         + a₄ · z²         (L₋ = σ₁σ₀)\n         + a₅ · (h·z² + z) (e⁻ = σ₀σ₁σ₀)\n\nThe values come from the Markov axioms applied to each basis\nelement individually:\n  • tr(γ) = 1            by (M3)\n  • tr(σ_i) = z          by (M2) with x = γ\n  • tr(σ_iσ_j) = z²      by two (M2) peels (`prop:markov-pair-z2`)\n  • tr(σ_iσ_jσ_i) = h·z² + z (Hecke quadratic + Markov peel)\n\nCorrected 2026-09-05 (`qou-46ab`): this claimed the Python\nproduction witnesses cross-check the formula at `q = q₀` to\n≤ 4·10⁻¹⁶ against the Hoefsmit + Wenzl bridge. That tolerance was\nmeasured in **convention C** and does not hold as stated; the\nbridge witness is 7·10⁻² from the C-frame value. The formula\nitself is convention-independent — it is the Markov axioms applied\nbasis element by basis element — so nothing above depends on `z`'s\nvalue. The numeric claim is dropped rather than restated with a new\ntolerance, because it has not been re-measured under D.\n\nThe signature takes an explicit ring hom `φ : R_q →+* R`\n(the \"lift\" of the algebra coefficients into the trace ring)\nso the canonical instance with `R = R_q` and `φ = RingHom.id`\ndrops out trivially, while the symbolic instance with\n`R = R_q[z, z⁻¹] / (z⁻¹ − (q² + 1)/q³)` is also expressible via\nthe inclusion hom.  (Corrected 2026-09-05, `qou-46ab`: the defining\nrelation read `z⁻¹ − q^{1/2} − q^{-1/2}`, i.e. **convention C**.\nUnder production convention D, `z = q³/(q²+1)`, so the relation is\n`z⁻¹ = (q²+1)/q³` — and note it needs no √q, which is one of the\nstructural reasons D is the production trace.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.MarkovTraceH3.tr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.MarkovTraceH3.tr","kind":"def","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/MarkovPeelH3.lean#L103-L103","doc":"The trace map.  Linear in the NF basis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.MarkovTraceH3.h","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.MarkovTraceH3.h","kind":"def","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/MarkovPeelH3.lean#L101-L101","doc":"The Hecke parameter `h = q − q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.MarkovTraceH3.z","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.MarkovTraceH3.z","kind":"def","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/MarkovPeelH3.lean#L99-L99","doc":"The Markov parameter `z = q³/(q²+1) = q²/[2]_q` — **convention D**,\nthe production trace (trace-convention registry). Corrected\n2026-09-05 (`qou-46ab`): this read `z = 1/(q^{1/2} + q^{-1/2})`,\nwhich is **convention C**, excised by the owner ruling of\n2026-08-09. The two are not variant normalisations of one\nquantity — see `rem:markov-z-reconciliation`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.MarkovTraceH3.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.MarkovTraceH3.mk","kind":"ctor","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/MarkovPeelH3.lean#L92-L92","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.MarkovTraceH3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.MarkovTraceH3","kind":"structure","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/MarkovPeelH3.lean#L87-L103","doc":"An H₃-specific Markov-trace structure parameterised on the\ntarget ring `R` (typically a √q-extended Laurent ring or a\nformal symbolic ring).  Captures the canonical trace on the\nsix NF basis elements of H₃(q):\n{γ, σ₀, σ₁, L₊, L₋, e⁻}. ","signatureChunk":0}]}